        "original_id": "d2a074f8-d068-51ac-8e51-53a4f9694e51",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Hensley Meulens, Andruw Jones, Robert Eenhoorn\n- Places: Curaçao, the Netherlands, the Caribbean territories\n- Organizations: San Francisco Giants, Major League Baseball, Nippon Professional Baseball, Korea Baseball Organization, Dominican Professional Baseball League\n- Roles: baseball player, hitting coach\n\nFacts:\n- Hensley Meulens was born on June 23, 1967.\n- Hensley Meulens is a native of Curaçao.\n- Hensley Meulens is a retired Dutch professional baseball player and a hitting coach for the San Francisco Giants.\n- Hensley Meulens played from 1989 to 2000 in Major League Baseball, Nippon Professional Baseball, and the Korea Baseball Organization.\n- Hensley Meulens was the first Curaçaoan to play in both Major League Baseball and the Dominican Professional Baseball League.\n- Hensley Meulens speaks English, Spanish, Dutch, Papiamento, and Japanese.\n- The other Dutch Major League Baseball players who hit home runs were born outside the European Netherlands, mainly in the country's Caribbean territories.\n- Andruw Jones and Hensley Meulens are notable Curaçao-born Dutch Major League Baseball players who hit home runs.",
